  "security_implications": "This block aggregates security‑critical error and fault indicators: FSM consistency, register/shadow‑storage integrity, key ECC, side‑channel FSM anomalies, counter errors, and reseed counter errors. The outputs fault_o and error_o are used to decide whether to abort key‑manager operations or trigger key destruction. Masking faults due to op_done_i gating or sticky‑bit handling could allow continued operation under compromised conditions, potentially exposing secret key material or reducing side‑channel resistance. Any missed or mis‑routed fault directly undermines the key manager’s security guarantees.",
